# Result: 02-schema (telemetry-benchmark)

test_command=sh tests/bench-harness_test.sh
id=schema-01 result=green reason=test_schema_01 (two repetitions append two lines; each parses standalone via the suite's own character-scanner and its key sequence equals the pinned field set exactly once in pinned order) + test_schema_01_closed (missing field, extra field, duplicate field, malformed line, empty input all refused with the JSONL never created or touched)
id=schema-02 result=green reason=test_schema_02 (wall_clock_ms emitted as bare >= 0 even for a timed-out run, null wall clock or negative wall clock refused; the nine metrics plus client_duration_ms emitted null-never-0 and 0-never-null, negative metric refused; models_used and slug carried verbatim comma-joined or null; string values with quotes/backslashes survive as valid JSON)
id=schema-03 result=green reason=test_schema_03_precedence (all six outcomes classified in the pinned first-match order with every higher-vs-lower pair exercised, empty archive/ is not approval, kill flag only decides when no disk evidence matches) + test_schema_03_disk_only (client prose in the repo root, result=blocked in a non-receipt file, a single-digit-name receipt file, green receipts, and "BLOCKED:" without the pinned ": " are all non-evidence)
id=schema-04 result=green reason=test_schema_04 (verifier_rejections counts only line-start "## Rejection " headings, subspecs_declared/subspecs_receipted count only top-level NN-* files summed across change dirs, all three bare integers with 0 on absent change dir/REJECTED.md, bench_observed_slug null | solo | comma-joined sorted)
id=schema-05 result=green reason=test_schema_05 (three repetitions with a failing middle still append three lines; the failed record is complete: outcome error, all twelve telemetry fields null, exit_code 7 carried, error_note the reason, wall clock measured; timeout-with-note accepted; error_note-on-approved, error/timeout-without-note, and an out-of-vocabulary outcome all refused)

Notes for later sub-specs (contract surfaces this receipt pins):
- bench/lib.sh schema section: bench_schema_fields (pinned 28-name field set,
  one per line, THE source of truth for order), bench_emit_record
  <jsonl-file> reading "key=value" lines on stdin (exactly one per pinned
  field; literal "null" means unavailable -- the same token bench_collect
  prints per bench-adapter), bench_outcome_classify <repo-dir>
  <killed:0|1> printing one outcome, bench_change_dirs, bench_observed_slug,
  bench_count_declared / bench_count_receipted / bench_count_rejections
  (take the repo dir, print a bare integer).
- bench_emit_record validates whole and appends all-or-nothing: unknown,
  duplicate, missing, or malformed lines; never-null fields (run_id,
  timestamp, client, antz_version, scenario, repetition, wall_clock_ms,
  the three counters, exit_code -- exit_code null is refused because every
  record's client ran); metric types (null or integer >= 0, cost_usd null or
  decimal >= 0); outcome vocabulary; and the error_note non-null <=>
  outcome in {error,timeout} rule. A refusal exits non-zero and creates or
  modifies NOTHING -- runner-04's "harness-internal failure" path can treat
  an emit refusal as fatal before/while writing.
- JSON types are per-field pinned (numbers emitted bare), NOT inferred, so
  e.g. a version string is always quoted.
- Classification evidence: receipts are NN-*.result at the top level of a
  change dir (substring "result=blocked" in a line); the refusal marker is
  any file at any depth under spdd/changes/<slug>/ with a line-start
  "BLOCKED: " (colon+space); REJECTED.md and OPEN_QUESTIONS.md are looked
  for at change-dir top level; approved needs a DIRECTORY under
  spdd/archive/. With several change dirs the evidence unions across them
  and the counters sum (the singular "the change dir" phrasing with the
  plural slug field read as one-vs-many flow outputs).
- The timeout input is a "1"/"0" flag -- the runner's own kill record lives
  in the run dir per bench-adapter; the schema stays agnostic about its
  file name.
- Tests exercise the schema at the bench/lib.sh seam (canned kv sets,
  canned artifact trees); the full "runner completes repetitions with the
  dry-run client" loop is re-pinned by bench-adapter (adapter-04..07) and
  bench-runner (runner-03) over these same functions.
- Suite stays hermetic: JSON validity is checked by the suite's own awk
  character-scanner (no jq/python/node anywhere); sh -n and bash --posix -n
  parse bench/lib.sh clean.
